      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "RUSTY PATCH (1) stuck on well last time to finish 2 lengths back in second (23.03) at this track in a Grade 5 over 401m. Reliable out of the boxes and should take advantage of the inside draw. One of the contenders. PARISIAN JET (4) generally breaks well and with clear running can clear the draw. Last start finished 4th over 401m at this track beaten 5.5 lengths (23.26) behind Going Broke in a Grade 5 on October 25. Can feature in the finish. CHINESE CHARIOT (2) went straight to the front and never headed when winning by a space two back but could manage only midfield last time when finished 4th and beaten 6 lengths at Nowra (21.17). Good beginner aided by a nice draw. Expected to feature in the finish. ALLY'S CRITTER (6) has ability and finds the right scenario to bounce back.",
